<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabaré Vázquez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/2020">2020</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tabaré Vázquez was a Uruguayan oncologist and politician of the Broad Front, the first left-wing president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>. As mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montevideo">Montevideo</a> from 1990 to 1995 he built the coalition's base, and he served as president in 2005–2010 and 2015–2020. His governments expanded social spending and introduced strict tobacco-control laws.</p></div>
